# Copy to tests/windows/hosts.env and fill in, then `set -a; . tests/windows/hosts.env; set +a`.
# Never commit a real hosts.env. The gate reads these; the user (not an agent) edits them.
#
# The gate sets ZB_GUEST_USER per host from ZB_WIN11_USER / ZB_WIN10_USER before probing/staging that
# host, and selects the matching per-host key + known_hosts, so the two hosts can use different accounts
# and pinned host keys. All Windows work stays under C:\Users\<user>\zb\; tests never touch the file
# server's shares and never run tests/guest/setup.ps1.

# --- Win11 VM (build + run), reached via the local libvirt passt forward (127.0.0.1:2222) ---
# Verified 2026-10-19: Win11 25H2 build 26200, x64, WebView2 155.0.4283.62, user zbtext (standard).
ZB_WIN11_HOST=127.0.0.1
ZB_WIN11_PORT=2222
ZB_WIN11_DOMAIN=win11-m8
ZB_WIN11_USER=zbtext
ZB_WIN11_KEY=/home/maceo/vms/win11-m8/zb_win_key
ZB_WIN11_KNOWN_HOSTS=/home/maceo/vms/win11-m8/known_hosts

# --- Toolchain on the Win11 VM (bead zigBrowser-4dr, option B: MACHINE-WIDE install under C:\tools) ---
# The user installs these as admin on the VM console (exact PowerShell in the session morning-brief):
#   zig 0.16.0          -> C:\tools\zig\zig.exe
#   WebView2 SDK nuget  -> C:\tools\webview2  (headers at build\native\include, x64 import libs at
#                          build\native\x64), readable+executable by all users (icacls Users:(RX)).
# build-on-windows.sh DEFAULTS to exactly these paths, so these three are OPTIONAL — set them only to
# point at an off-standard install. MSVC (VS18 BuildTools) + the Windows SDK are already machine-wide.
#ZB_ZIG=C:\tools\zig\zig.exe
#ZB_WEBVIEW2_INCLUDE=C:\tools\webview2\build\native\include
#ZB_WEBVIEW2_LIB=C:\tools\webview2\build\native\x64

# --- Windows 10 file server (run only), tailnet file-server-win-mac ---
# Verified 2026-10-20 (read-only probe from this host): Windows 10 version 2004, build 19041, x64,
# WebView2 155.0.4283.62 present (Evergreen supports 2004), user zbtest (standard: Users / Medium
# integrity, not Administrators), C:\Users\zbtest\zb not yet created.
# sshd: OpenSSH_for_Windows_8.1; ListenAddress 100.123.34.15; AllowUsers zbtest; authorized_keys is
#   from="100.78.56.108",restrict,pty  (reachable only from this Linux host).
# Host key (ed25519, confirmed by the user):
#   SHA256:AhusOW2s/1hKVAOhriqN38c1Hn8hSiNMBrdbcRGAnF4
# RULES on this machine: install nothing without the orchestrator; never touch the shares; never run
# tests/guest/setup.ps1; keep all work under C:\Users\zbtest\zb\.
ZB_WIN10_HOST=100.123.34.15
ZB_WIN10_PORT=22
ZB_WIN10_USER=zbtest
ZB_WIN10_KEY=/home/maceo/vms/win11-m8/zb_win_key
ZB_WIN10_KNOWN_HOSTS=/home/maceo/vms/win10-fs/known_hosts

# --- Compatibility: the current single-host code (gate.sh ssh_opts, resolve_path.sh) reads these and
# defaults to the VM. The two-host gate run selects the per-host key/known_hosts above. ---
ZB_WIN_KEY=/home/maceo/vms/win11-m8/zb_win_key
ZB_WIN_KNOWN_HOSTS=/home/maceo/vms/win11-m8/known_hosts
